Summary: configure finds macOS's PCSC framework again (smart cards)
Category: build
Kind: fix
Origin: winehq
  Commit: e5c902a41ff7c0f8dcd546b1564c11117da5185d
  URL: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/e5c902a41ff7c0f8dcd546b1564c11117da5185d
  Authors: Sven Baars
  Changes: verbatim (configure and configure.ac, as committed)
Upstream: yes (Wine 11.13)
Needed until: 11.13 (WineHQ has the commit from then)
Why: 11.12 moved configure's libpcsclite check to WINE_PACKAGE_FLAGS, where
 the macOS fallback to -framework PCSC sits in an argument that never runs
 when the function check fails. So on macOS PCSCLITE_LIBS stays empty, and
 with --with-pcsclite (flavours/wine.sh) configure stops: "libpcsclite not
 found, smart cards won't be supported". 11.11 and earlier, and 11.13 and
 later, find the framework. The patch sets it in the check's failure case.
 It doesn't change what Wine does at run time: winscard is built against
 the PCSC framework as in every other version.
Programs: none (build)
No test: build only; wine 11.12 build1 (CI run 46146369192) stopped in
 configure without it
Status: 11.12: 2026-11-28: written; not yet in a build

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 186641c73a9..1834f20d30d 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -17276,7 +17276,10 @@ if test "x$ac_cv_func_SCardEstablishContext" = xyes
 then :
   :
 else case e in #(
-  e) PCSCLITE_LIBS="" ;;
+  e) case $host_os in
+                        darwin*) PCSCLITE_LIBS="-framework PCSC" ;;
+                        *) PCSCLITE_LIBS="";;
+                     esac ;;
 esac
 fi
 
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index b11bfefa3dc..ee0b1c483d4 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1522,10 +1522,11 @@ dnl **** Check for libpcsclite ****
 if test "x$with_pcsclite" != "xno"
 then
     WINE_PACKAGE_FLAGS(PCSCLITE,[libpcsclite],[-lpcsclite],,,
-                 [AC_CHECK_FUNC(SCardEstablishContext,[:],[PCSCLITE_LIBS=""])],
-                 [case $host_os in
-                    darwin*) AC_SUBST(PCSCLITE_LIBS,"-framework PCSC") ;;
-                  esac])
+                 [AC_CHECK_FUNC(SCardEstablishContext,[:],
+                    [case $host_os in
+                        darwin*) PCSCLITE_LIBS="-framework PCSC" ;;
+                        *) PCSCLITE_LIBS="";;
+                     esac])])
 fi
 WINE_NOTICE_WITH(pcsclite,[test "x$PCSCLITE_LIBS" = x],
                  [libpcsclite not found, smart cards won't be supported.],
